//! 📦️ Package glue — wiring only. Domain lives at the owner `🦀️component.rs` files.

// 🔀️ R3/R7 (dedyn-fw-server): `async fn` in a public trait warns because auto trait bounds
// (`Send`) cannot be named on it — answered STRUCTURALLY here, not by the compiler's suggested
// `+ Send`. Every former `dyn <Trait>` seam in this crate (`Decider`, `PrincipalResolver`,
// `QueryHandler`, `DocumentAuthority`, `Saga`, `ServerModule`, `AuthorityStore`, `ProjectionStore`,
// `BlobStore`, `SessionStore`) now closes over a concrete enum generated by
// `dyn_enum`/`dyn_enum_close!` (`semio-framework-dispatch-macros`), so the concrete type at each
// call site is always known and `Send` (where it matters) falls out on its own. Never resolve this
// lint by adding `+ Send` to a trait method or by making it sync.
#![allow(async_fn_in_trait)]

